{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-35-1","title":"Psalms 35:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 David prays for his own safety, and his enemies confusion. 11 He complains of their wrongful dealing. 22 Thereby he incites God against them.</p>\n<p>A.M. 2942. B.C. 1062. Plead. 43:1; 119:154; 1Sa 24:15; Pr 22:23; 23:11; Jer 51:36; La 3:58 Mic 7:9 fight. Ex 14:25; Jos 10:42; Ne 4:20; Ac 5:39; 23:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-2","title":"Psalms 35:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>7:12,13; Ex 15:3; De 32:41,42; Isa 13:5; 42:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-3","title":"Psalms 35:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>stop. 27:2; 76:10; 1Sa 23:26,27; Job 1:10; Isa 8:9,10; 10:12; Ac 4:28 say. 51:12; 62:7; 91:16; Ge 49:18; Isa 12:2; Lu 2:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-4","title":"Psalms 35:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>confounded. 26; 31:17,18; 40:14,15; 70:2,3; 71:24 that. 38:12; 1Sa 23:23; 1Ki 19:10; Eze 13:19; Mt 27:1 turned. 129:5; Isa 37:29; Jer 46:5; Joh 18:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-5","title":"Psalms 35:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>as chaff. 1:4; 83:13-17; Job 21:18; Isa 17:13; 29:5; Ho 13:3 and. Ex 14:19; Isa 37:36; Ac 12:23; Heb 11:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-6","title":"Psalms 35:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>their. 73:18; Pr 4:19; Jer 13:16; 23:12 dark and slippery. Heb. darkness and slipperiness.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-7","title":"Psalms 35:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>without. 7:3-5; 25:3; 64:4; Joh 15:25 hid. 9:15; 119:85; 140:5; Job 18:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-8","title":"Psalms 35:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Let destruction.All the verbs in these verses, (ver. 4-8,) in the original, are in the future tense, as a prediction, and should probably be so rendered; though as that tense is frequently used in Hebrew for the imperative, most translators, both ancient and modern, have considered them as an imprecation.</p>\n<p>64:7; 73:18-20; Pr 29:1; Lu 21:34; 1Th 5:3 at unawares. Heb. which he knoweth not of. net. 7:15,16; 57:6; 141:9,10; Pr 5:22 into. 1Sa 18:17; 31:2-4; 2Sa 17:2-4,23; 18:14,15; Es 7:10; Mt 27:3-5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-9","title":"Psalms 35:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>13:5; 21:1; 33:21; 48:11; 58:10,11; 68:1-3; 1Sa 2:1; Isa 61:10 Hab 3:18; Lu 1:46,47; Ga 5:22; Php 3:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-10","title":"Psalms 35:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>All. 22:14; 32:3; 34:20; 38:3; 51:8; 102:3; Job 33:19-25 who. 71:19; 86:8; 89:6-8; Ex 15:11; Isa 40:18,25; Jer 10:7 which. 10:14; 22:24; 34:6; 69:33; 102:17-20; 109:31; 140:12; Job 5:15,16 Pr 22:22,23 too. 18:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-11","title":"Psalms 35:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>False witnesses. Heb. Witnesses of wrong. 27:12; 1Sa 24:9; 25:10; Mt 26:59,60; Ac 6:13; 24:5,6,12,13 laid, etc. Heb. asked me.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-12","title":"Psalms 35:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>They. 38:20; 109:3-5; 1Sa 19:4,5,15; 22:13,14; Pr 17:13; Jer 18:20 Joh 10:32 spoiling. Heb. depriving. 1Sa 20:31-33; Lu 23:21-23 my soul.Or, \"my life,\" as the word {nephesh} frequently denotes.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-13","title":"Psalms 35:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>when. 69:10,11; Job 30:25; Mt 5:44; Ro 12:14,15 humbled. or, afflicted. Le 16:29,31; 1Ki 21:27-29; Isa 58:3,5; Mt 9:14,15 my prayer. Mt 10:13; Lu 10:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-14","title":"Psalms 35:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>I behaved, etc. Heb. I walked as a friend, as brother to me.I bowed. 2Sa 1:11,12,17-27; Lu 19:41,42 as one.Or, \"as a mourning mother,\" {k�avel aim.}</p>\n<p>Ge 24:67</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-15","title":"Psalms 35:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>in mine. 25,26; 41:8; 71:10,11; Job 31:29; Pr 17:5; 24:17,18 adversity. Heb. halting. 38:17; Jer 20:10; 1Co 13:6 the abjects. 22:16; 69:12; Job 30:1-12; Mt 27:27-30,39-44; Mr 14:65; Ac 17:5 I knew. 8; *marg: they. 7:2; 57:4; Job 16:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-16","title":"Psalms 35:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>hypocritical. 1Sa 20:24-42; Isa 1:14,15; Joh 18:28; 1Co 5:8 gnashed. 37:12; Job 16:9; La 2:16; Ac 7:54</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-17","title":"Psalms 35:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>how. 6:3; 13:1,2; 74:9,10; 89:46; 94:3,4 look. 10:14; Hab 1:13 rescue. 22:20,21; 57:4; 69:14,15; 142:6,7 darling. Heb. only one.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-18","title":"Psalms 35:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>give. 22:22-25,31; 40:9,10; 69:30-34; 111:1; 116:14,18; Heb 2:12 praise. 67:1-4; 117:1,2; 138:4,5; Ro 15:9 much. Heb. strong. Isa 25:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-19","title":"Psalms 35:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Let. 15; 13:4; 25:2; 38:16; Joh 16:20-22; Re 11:7-10 wrongfully. Heb. falsely. 38:19 wink. Job 15:12; Pr 6:13; 10:10 that hate. 69:4; 109:3; 119:161; 1Sa 24:11,12; La 3:52; Joh 15:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-20","title":"Psalms 35:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>For. 120:5-7 but. 31:13; 36:3,4; 38:12; 52:2; 64:4-6; 140:2-5; Jer 11:19; Da 6:5 Mt 26:4; Ac 23:15; 25:3 quiet. Mt 12:19,24; 1Pe 2:22,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-21","title":"Psalms 35:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>Yea. 22:13; Isa 9:12; Lu 11:53,54 Aha. 40:15; 54:7; 70:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-22","title":"Psalms 35:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>This. Ex 3:7; Ac 7:34 keep. 28:1; 39:12; 50:21; 83:1 be. 10:1; 22:11,19; 38:21; 71:12; Isa 65:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-23","title":"Psalms 35:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Stir. 7:6; 44:23; 80:2; Isa 51:9 my God. 89:26; 142:5; Joh 20:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-24","title":"Psalms 35:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Judge. 7:8; 18:20-24; 26:1; 43:1; 2Th 1:6; 1Pe 2:22 and let. 19; Job 20:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-25","title":"Psalms 35:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>say. 27:12; 28:3; 70:3; 74:8; Job 1:5; Mr 2:6,8 Ah. Heb. Ah, Ah, our soul. so. 140:8; Ex 15:9; Mt 27:43 We have. 56:1,2; 57:3; 124:3; 2Sa 20:19; La 2:16; 1Co 15:54</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-26","title":"Psalms 35:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>ashamed. 4; 40:14,15; 71:13; 129:5; 132:18; Isa 41:11; 65:13-15 clothed. 109:28,29; 132:18; Job 8:22; 1Pe 5:5 magnify. 38:16; 55:12; Job 19:5; Jer 48:26; Da 11:36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-27","title":"Psalms 35:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>shout. 40:16; 68:3; 132:9,16; 142:7; Isa 66:10,11; Joh 16:22; Ro 12:15 1Co 12:26 righteous cause. Heb. righteousness. Pr 8:18 say. 70:4 which. 149:4; Jer 32:40,41; Zep 3:14,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-35-28","title":"Psalms 35:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":35,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":35,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>34:1; 50:15; 51:14,15; 71:24; 104:33,34; 145:1,2,5,21</p>"}]}